  "problem": "Find the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{\u2016v\u2016\\,\u2016w\u2016},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+(-\\sqrt{5})\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 5+1\\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{\\sqrt{64}\\cdot \\sqrt{32}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
